course: dictionary
lesson: 11105
title: One word, three jobs: while
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word while has three main jobs in a sentence. It can mean at the same time as, it can show a difference, and it can name a stretch of time. The words around it tell you which job it is doing.
explain: «A boy in California crossed a street while looking at his phone.» Here while means at the same time as: he was crossing the street and looking at his phone together. Ask yourself if both things happen at once. If they do, while means at the same time as.
explain: «Slow blinks mean a cat feels safe with you, while wide, round pupils in good light can mean it is scared or excited.» Here while shows a difference between two things, a bit like but. The two facts sit side by side so the reader can compare them.
explain: The word also appears in phrases. «A while» is a noun meaning some time, often not long. «To while away» time is a verb meaning to pass it in a relaxed way. Check the words before and after while to see which job it has.
fact: While means at the same time as, as in «while looking at his phone».
fact: While can mean but or although, to show a difference, as in «while wide, round pupils in good light».
fact: «A while» is a noun meaning some time, often not long, as in «once in a while».
fact: To «while away» time is to pass it in a relaxed way.
fact: In UK writing you may also see whilst, which means the same as while.
exercise: «The same piece has three names: a meteoroid while it is in space, a meteor while it glows in the air, and a meteorite if any of it lands on the ground.» In «a meteor while it glows in the air», what does while mean? | Although | Some time, often not long | To pass time in a relaxed way | *At the same time as
exercise: «Editing means improving the writing, while proofreading means hunting the small slips.» What does while show here? | Some time, often not long | *A difference between two things | Passing time in a relaxed way | Two things happening at the same time
exercise: Mum says, «Wait a while.» What does a while mean? | At the same time as something else | To pass time in a relaxed way | *Some time, often not long | A difference between two things
test: Amira likes to while away the hours with a book on a rainy day. What does while away mean? | Lose track of where she is | Hurry through time as fast as possible | Waste money on something silly | *Pass time in a relaxed way
test: Tom is tired, while his sister is full of energy. What is while showing? | To pass time in a relaxed way | At the same time as | Some time, often not long | *A difference between two things
exam: «The fox crept closer while the hen slept.» What is the job of while here? | Some time, often not long | To pass time in a relaxed way | *At the same time as | A difference between two things
